## Diseño Detallado del AST (Fase 3)

### Jerarquía de Nodos

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class ASTNode {
        <<sealed interface>>
        +accept(ASTVisitor visitor) Object
        +int line()
        +int column()
    }

    class NumberNode {
        +double value
        +boolean isInteger
    }

    class BoolNode {
        +boolean value
    }

    class StringNode {
        +String value
    }

    class VariableNode {
        +String name
    }

    class BinOpNode {
        +ASTNode left
        +TokenType operator
        +ASTNode right
    }

    class UnaryOpNode {
        +TokenType operator
        +ASTNode operand
    }

    class AssignNode {
        +String name
        +ASTNode value
    }

    class FuncDefNode {
        +String name
        +List~String~ params
        +BlockNode body
    }

    class FuncCallNode {
        +String name
        +List~ASTNode~ arguments
    }

    class IfNode {
        +ASTNode condition
        +BlockNode thenBranch
        +BlockNode elseBranch
    }

    class WhileNode {
        +ASTNode condition
        +BlockNode body
    }

    class PrintNode {
        +ASTNode expression
    }

    class ReturnNode {
        +ASTNode value
    }

    class BlockNode {
        +List~ASTNode~ statements
    }

    ASTNode <|.. NumberNode
    ASTNode <|.. BoolNode
    ASTNode <|.. StringNode
    ASTNode <|.. VariableNode
    ASTNode <|.. BinOpNode
    ASTNode <|.. UnaryOpNode
    ASTNode <|.. AssignNode
    ASTNode <|.. FuncDefNode
    ASTNode <|.. FuncCallNode
    ASTNode <|.. IfNode
    ASTNode <|.. WhileNode
    ASTNode <|.. PrintNode
    ASTNode <|.. ReturnNode
    ASTNode <|.. BlockNode
```

### Definición Java de los Nodos

Usaremos **Java Records** (Java 17+) para los nodos del AST, ya que son inmutables y concisos:

```java
// Interfaz base sellada
public sealed interface ASTNode
    permits NumberNode, BoolNode, StringNode, VariableNode,
            BinOpNode, UnaryOpNode, AssignNode, FuncDefNode,
            FuncCallNode, IfNode, WhileNode, PrintNode,
            ReturnNode, BlockNode {
    
    int line();
    int column();
    <T> T accept(ASTVisitor<T> visitor);
}

// Ejemplo: BinOpNode
public record BinOpNode(
    ASTNode left,
    TokenType operator,
    ASTNode right,
    int line,
    int column
) implements ASTNode {
    @Override
    public <T> T accept(ASTVisitor<T> visitor) {
        return visitor.visitBinOp(this);
    }
}
```

### Visitor Interface

```java
public interface ASTVisitor<T> {
    T visitNumber(NumberNode node);
    T visitBool(BoolNode node);
    T visitString(StringNode node);
    T visitVariable(VariableNode node);
    T visitBinOp(BinOpNode node);
    T visitUnaryOp(UnaryOpNode node);
    T visitAssign(AssignNode node);
    T visitFuncDef(FuncDefNode node);
    T visitFuncCall(FuncCallNode node);
    T visitIf(IfNode node);
    T visitWhile(WhileNode node);
    T visitPrint(PrintNode node);
    T visitReturn(ReturnNode node);
    T visitBlock(BlockNode node);
}
```

