## Diseño del Parser Recursivo Descendente (Fase 3)

### Gramática LL(1) — Mapeo a Métodos

Cada regla de producción de la gramática EBNF se mapea a un método del parser:

| Producción EBNF | Método Java | Descripción |
|---|---|---|
| `program → statement*` | `parseProgram()` | Punto de entrada |
| `statement → assignStmt \| funcDef \| ifStmt \| whileStmt \| printStmt \| returnStmt \| exprStmt` | `parseStatement()` | Despacho por token actual |
| `assignStmt → 'let' ID '=' expr` | `parseAssign()` | Declaración de variable |
| `funcDef → 'def' ID '(' params ')' '{' block '}'` | `parseFuncDef()` | Definición de función |
| `ifStmt → 'if' expr '{' block '}' ('else' '{' block '}')?` | `parseIf()` | Condicional |
| `whileStmt → 'while' expr '{' block '}'` | `parseWhile()` | Ciclo |
| `printStmt → 'print' '(' expr ')'` | `parsePrint()` | Salida |
| `returnStmt → 'return' expr` | `parseReturn()` | Retorno |
| `block → statement*` | `parseBlock()` | Bloque de sentencias |
| `expr → orExpr` | `parseExpression()` | Entrada a expresiones |
| `orExpr → andExpr ('or' andExpr)*` | `parseOr()` | OR lógico |
| `andExpr → comparison ('and' comparison)*` | `parseAnd()` | AND lógico |
| `comparison → addition (('==' \| '!=' \| '<' \| '>' \| '<=' \| '>=') addition)*` | `parseComparison()` | Comparaciones |
| `addition → multiplication (('+' \| '-') multiplication)*` | `parseAddition()` | Suma/Resta |
| `multiplication → power (('*' \| '/' \| '%') power)*` | `parseMultiplication()` | Multiplicación/División |
| `power → unary ('^' unary)*` | `parsePower()` | Potenciación |
| `unary → ('-' \| 'not') unary \| call` | `parseUnary()` | Negación |
| `call → primary ('(' arguments ')')?` | `parseCall()` | Llamada a función |
| `primary → NUMBER \| STRING \| BOOL \| ID \| '(' expr ')'` | `parsePrimary()` | Literales y agrupación |

### Precedencia de Operadores (menor a mayor)

```
1. or
2. and
3. ==  !=  <  >  <=  >=
4. +  -
5. *  /  %
6. ^
7. not  - (unario)
8. llamada a función
9. literales / paréntesis
```

### Estructura del Parser

```java
public class Parser {
    private final List<Token> tokens;
    private int current = 0;
    private final List<ParseError> errors = new ArrayList<>();

    public Parser(List<Token> tokens) {
        this.tokens = tokens;
    }

    public BlockNode parse() {
        return parseProgram();
    }

    // --- Métodos auxiliares ---
    private Token peek()       { return tokens.get(current); }
    private Token previous()   { return tokens.get(current - 1); }
    private boolean isAtEnd()  { return peek().type() == TokenType.EOF; }
    private Token advance()    { if (!isAtEnd()) current++; return previous(); }
    
    private boolean check(TokenType type) {
        return !isAtEnd() && peek().type() == type;
    }
    
    private boolean match(TokenType... types) {
        for (TokenType type : types) {
            if (check(type)) { advance(); return true; }
        }
        return false;
    }
    
    private Token consume(TokenType type, String message) {
        if (check(type)) return advance();
        throw error(peek(), message);
    }

    // --- Métodos de parsing (uno por producción) ---
    private BlockNode parseProgram() { ... }
    private ASTNode parseStatement() { ... }
    // ... etc
}
```

